<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Ensor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1860–1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Ensor was a Belgian painter and printmaker from Ostend, a forerunner of expressionism. He was a member of the avant-garde group Les XX, and his works, filled with masks, skeletons and crowds, mocked bourgeois society. His best-known painting, &quot;Christ's Entry into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> in 1889&quot;, completed in 1888, is now in the J. Paul Getty Museum. He was made a baron in 1929.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-ensor.jpg" alt="James Ensor" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Ensor · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ensor_voor_zijn_schildersezel,_James_Ensor,_1890,_Koninklijk_Museum_voor_Schone_Kunsten_Antwerpen,_2809.001.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
